# Chapter 4: Branches and Pull Requests

## 4.1 Introduction

GitHub allows people to work on projects together. When several people work on the same project, they need a way to make changes without affecting the main version of the project.

Branches and pull requests help users work in an organized way.

In this chapter, you will learn how to:

- Understand branches
- Create a branch
- Make changes on a branch
- Create a pull request
- Review changes
- Merge a pull request
- Understand basic collaboration

---

## 4.2 What Is a Branch?

A **branch** is a separate version of a project.

Branches allow you to make changes without changing the main version of the project immediately.

For example, imagine that you have a documentation project called `github-guide`.

The main branch contains the current version of the guide. You can create another branch to work on a new chapter.

